# HomeAsset — agent rules

Phone-first home memory for **homeowners only** — no in-app contractor mode/face. Contractors use LightLift; non-LightLift pros get a homeowner-sent invite link later. **Homeowners own the record.** Stack: Expo (React Native) + optional Hono API + Supabase Postgres with RLS.

## Prefer LightLift patterns

- **Auth → account bootstrap:** after signup/sign-in when a session exists, call the security-definer RPC `bootstrap_new_user` (client-driven). Do **not** ship Auth SQL triggers as the only way to create profiles. Build the right pattern first even if slower.
- **Cloud phone path:** Supabase URL + anon key only — no laptop/localhost API and no LAN IP required for preview signup/core ledger once configured.
- **AI keys:** edge/server secrets only (`GEMINI_API_KEY` preferred, same name as LightLift). Never put AI or service-role keys in `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` or on the device.

## Security first

- RLS on every homeowner ledger table; least privilege.
- Users may only bootstrap / read / update **their own** profile (`auth.uid()`). No broad insert policies that let one user create another’s profile.
- No service-role key on the phone. Parameterized queries / bound RPC args only.
- Don’t trust the client for tenancy, ownership, or “official” writes.

## Privacy

- Homeowner control; least data shared.
- Approve-before-official — no silent auto-adds to the ledger.
- Call out privacy tradeoffs when asking product decisions.

## Keep How to use in sync

- When you ship a **user-facing** feature (or move where it lives in the UI), update `apps/mobile/src/lib/settingsContent.ts` (`HOW_TO_USE_SECTIONS`, and Privacy/Security sections if promises change). That copy powers Settings → How to use / Privacy / Security.
- Home CTAs (top→bottom): **Ask HomeAsset** → **View Assets** → **Notifications** → **Settings**. AI is named Ask HomeAsset (`/ai/help`); no floating FAB when that home button exists.
- Do **not** put long instructional / privacy commentary on feature screens — How to use owns that. One Notifications surface for reminders + notices; delivery prefs stay under Settings.
- Colors: use shared tokens in `apps/mobile/src/lib/theme.ts` — no one-off palette drifts.
- “Suggest from permits” is not a primary CTA (off Home; no new home decided yet).

## Keep short

- Plain language for founder-facing notes (what to run in SQL Editor, whether a rebuild is needed).
- Strict TypeScript; Expo Router under `apps/mobile/src/app/`.
- Local SQLite remains the CI/demo default until Supabase secrets are set.
- Log failures with context; no silent `catch` on Auth/bootstrap.
